 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "some과 any",
   "en": "some and any"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "some은 긍정문에, any는 부정문과 의문문에 씁니다. 셀 수 없는 명사(milk, bread, rice)와 복수 명사(eggs, apples) 앞에 모두 쓸 수 있습니다. 권유나 부탁에는 의문문에서도 some을 씁니다: Would you like some water?",
   "en": "Use some in positive sentences and any in negatives and questions. Both go before uncountable nouns (milk, bread, rice) and plural nouns (eggs, apples). In offers and requests some is also used in questions: Would you like some water?"
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "some (긍정문)",
     "I have some bread."
    ],
    [
     "any (부정문)",
     "I don't have any milk."
    ],
    [
     "any (의문문)",
     "Do you have any eggs?"
    ],
    [
     "셀 수 없는 명사",
     "milk, bread, rice (-s 없음)"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "milk, bread, rice는 셀 수 없어서 -s를 붙이지 않습니다.",
    "en": "Milk, bread and rice are uncountable, so no -s."
   },
   {
    "ko": "There is + 셀 수 없는/단수, There are + 복수.",
    "en": "There is + uncountable/singular, There are + plural."
   },
   {
    "ko": "권유할 때는 some: Would you like some tea?",
    "en": "In offers use some: Would you like some tea?"
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
